 "headline": "On the 15800 least-cost cuttings of the single cell, every reading of the cycle-736 charge space is computed by the use-parity of a set of pieces, and the least such sets are measured. Every piece is used an odd number of times (1975), so a computing set's size has the parity of the reading: all eight readings force even size. A complete search of every set of at most eight pieces finds the smallest sets a cutting cannot see - 648 even octets - and the smallest computing the all-ones reading - 192 odd octets - while the six physical charges are carried by no set of eight or fewer and so need at least 10 pieces; verified sets of sizes 16 to 30 compute them. Both octet families are unions of orbits of the 48 cell symmetries with fixed geometry: the eight pieces of any octet share exactly two corners; for odd octets the shared pair is always a cell edge, six octets through each of the 32 edges; for even octets the shared pairs run over all 120 corner pairs with multiplicity set by the pair's distance alone.",
